      "name": "Thelia: Stored cross-site scripting vulnerability (CVE-2026-120205)",
      "description": "Thelia before 3.1.0 contains a stored cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability in the ForSomeCustomers::getSummary() method. Unauthenticated attackers can register with a script payload as their name. This script executes when administrators view related coupons, allowing the theft of CSRF tokens to create administrator accounts.\n",
